# Git workflow

## Branches

- Branch from up-to-date `main`. Never commit feature work directly on `main`.
- Name: `<type>/<short-kebab-description>`

| Type | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `feat/` | New user-facing capability |
| `fix/` | Bug fix |
| `chore/` | Tooling, deps, housekeeping |
| `docs/` | README / comments only |
| `refactor/` | No behavior change |
| `test/` | Tests only |
| `release/` | Version bump + changelog |

```text
✅ feat/ignore-list-persistence
✅ fix/restart-shell-metachar-check
❌ Feature/IgnoreList
❌ my-branch
```

- One concern per branch; prefer small PRs over long-lived branches.
- Delete the branch after merge.

## Commits

Use **Conventional Commits**: `<type>(optional-scope): <imperative summary>`

```text
✅ feat: detect Astro and Remix frameworks
✅ fix(actions): reject restart when command has metacharacters
✅ test: cover ListenerRow stop confirmation
❌ Fixed stuff / WIP / update
```

- Focus the message on **why**, not a file list.
- Do not commit `.env`, secrets, or `.build/` artifacts.
- Only create commits when the user asks.

## Pull requests

- Push with `-u` when the branch has no upstream yet.
- PR title matches the primary conventional commit theme.
- Body includes **Summary** (1–3 bullets) and **Test plan** (checklist).
- Do not force-push to `main`; avoid `--force` unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Do not merge or push unless the user asks.
